---One span row as the query and trace actions return it.
---
---The runner assembles these from HogQL result columns by position, so the key set is fixed even
---though the values come from a query. `trace_start` and `trace_duration` are the sort keys the
---trace list orders on, carried in the row rather than recomputed by the caller.
---@class posthog.tracing.Span
---@field uuid string Span's own UUID.
---@field trace_id string Trace this span belongs to.
---@field span_id string Span's ID within the trace.
---@field parent_span_id string Parent span's ID. Empty for a root span.
---@field name string Span name, which is the operation it represents.
---@field kind number OpenTelemetry span kind.
---@field service_name string Service that emitted the span.
---@field status_code number OpenTelemetry status code: 0 unset, 1 ok, 2 error.
---@field timestamp string When the span started.
---@field end_time string When the span ended.
---@field duration_nano number Span duration in nanoseconds.
---@field is_root_span boolean Whether the span has no parent in the trace.
---@field matched_filter number 1 when this span matched the request's filters, 0 when it is included as context. The query selects it as an expression, so it arrives as a number rather than a boolean.
---@field trace_start string Start of the whole trace, for ordering traces by recency.
---@field trace_duration number Duration of the whole trace in nanoseconds. Falls back to this span's duration.
---@field attributes posthog.tracing.SpanAttributesMap Span attributes. Keys are whatever the instrumentation set.
---@field resource_attributes posthog.tracing.SpanResourceAttributesMap Resource attributes of the emitting service. Keys are whatever the instrumentation set.

