---@class posthog.tracing.TracesRetentionRule
---@field id string Unique identifier for this retention rule.
---@field name string User-visible label for this rule.
---@field enabled? boolean When false, the rule is ignored by ingestion and listing UIs that show active rules only.
---@field priority? number|distilled.Null Lower numbers are evaluated first; the first matching rule wins. Omit to append after existing rules.
---@field config any Retention rule JSON. Required keys: `retention_days` (integer — how long matching logs are kept; must be a tier the organization is entitled to, same as the team-wide Logs retention setting) and `filter_group` (PropertyGroupFilter shape — an AND/OR tree of property predicates evaluated per record to decide which logs this rule matches). Example: `{"retention_days":30,"filter_group":{"type":"AND","values":[{"type":"AND","values":[{"key":"service.name","operator":"exact","value":"api"}]}]}}`. Logs matching no enabled rule keep the environment's default retention.
---@field version number Incremented on each update for worker cache coherency.
---@field created_by number
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string|distilled.Null

---@class posthog.tracing.TracingAggregationQueryBody
---@field dateRange? posthog.tracing.TracingDateRange Date range for the primary window. Defaults to last hour.
---@field compareFilter? posthog.tracing.CompareFilter Optional comparison-window configuration. When omitted, only the primary window is returned.
---@field serviceNames? posthog.tracing.TracingAggregationQueryBodyServiceNamesList Filter by service names.
---@field filterGroup? posthog.tracing.TracingAggregationQueryBodyFilterGroupList Property filters applied to spans in both windows.
---@field limit? number Max rows to return, ordered by total_duration_nano DESC. Defaults to 100; hard max 5000. Keep this small to bound the response size — a high value on high-cardinality span names (e.g. untemplated URL paths) returns a very large payload. Prefer narrowing with `serviceNames`/`filterGroup` over raising the limit.
---@field offset? number Row offset for pagination. Combine with `limit` and the `next_offset` returned in the response to page through results beyond the first page.
---@field includeImpact? boolean Also return the sessions and people behind each operation. Off by default because it reads the span and resource attribute maps, which the rest of the aggregation never touches.
---@field groupByEndpoint? boolean Group HTTP server spans by `METHOD route` (from `http.route`) in place of the span name, so raw paths like `/users/1` and `/users/2` fold into one row. Spans without a route keep their span name. Spans that are not HTTP server spans are left out.
---@field includeHealth? boolean Also return `health_status` and `health_reason` per row, comparing each row with the same row in the comparison window, or in the previous period when `compareFilter` is off. Uses the same statuses and thresholds as the service health check. Costs a second window query.

